title: Veeam: Backup Job (special agent)
agents: special
catalog: os/storage
license: GPLv2
distribution: check_mk
description:
 This check monitors the status of backup jobs reported by the Veeam
 Backup & Replication REST API, collected via the Veeam special agent.
 It reports the same information as the {VEEAM Job} service from the
 Veeam agent plug-in, and additionally reports the time since the last
 run, the next scheduled run, the target repository and the number of
 objects processed. The summary shows the result and the time since the
 last run, preceded by the status if the job is running or disabled.

 This check is {OK} if the result of the last run is Success. It is
 {WARN} if the result is Warning. It is {CRIT} if the result is Failed.
 A job with no result yet, either because it has never run or because a
 run is currently in progress, is {OK}. A disabled job is always {OK};
 its last result is shown for information only.

 A job that disappears from the API output makes the service {UNKNOWN}.

discovery:
 One service is created for each backup job reported by the API, including
 disabled ones. To leave out disabled jobs, disable this in the rule "Veeam:
 Backup job discovery".

item:
 The name of the backup job, sanitized: spaces and apostrophes are replaced
 by underscores.
